  "description": "Four forces act on a plane: thrust, drag, weight and lift. The curved, tilted wing deflects lots of air downward and the air pushes it up, with lower pressure above than below. The myth that the air over and under the wing arrives at the same time is false. A passenger jet takes off at about 250 km/h, cruises around 11 km up, and an aerobatic plane can fly upside down. Original 3D animation.",
